// Russian campaign — "Avdiivka": one motor-rifle brigade's sector of the 2023–24 Russian offensive on Avdiivka,
// from the opening pincer attacks of 10 October 2023 (north towards the coke-plant spoil heaps and Stepove, south
// towards Tsarska Okhota and Vodiane) through the industrial zone (November–December), the infiltration into southern
// Avdiivka (January), the second breach from the north-east and the cutting of the main supply road (February),
// to the Ukrainian withdrawal on 17 February 2024 and the coke plant. Plain data per schema.js.
//
// The BRIGADE IS FICTIONAL (219th Separate Motor Rifle Brigade) and so are its people: real formations fought here and
// attributing this unit's actions to any of them would misrepresent them. The GEOGRAPHY, the settlements, the roads,
// the railways, the industrial sites and the course of the operation are real and follow public reporting.
// Directive texts are paraphrased in-world orders, not quotations; no real person is named. The campaign depicts
// combat between armed forces only; it does not depict or reward harm to civilians or prisoners.
//
// Geography: OpenStreetMap (© OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL — https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright).
